the templates are:
    I will marry *a woman*; opposite I will not marry *a woman*.
    I love *a woman*.
    *a person* is a citizen; opposite *a person* is not a citizen.
    *a person* is born in *a country*.

the knowledge base only_if_test includes:

% Sufficient conditions
I will marry a woman if
    the woman is "Alice".
I will marry a woman if
    the woman is "Eve".

A person is a citizen if
    the person is born in a country.

% Necessary conditions (constraints)
I will marry a woman only if
    I love the woman.

A person is a citizen only if
    the person is born in "UK".

% Facts
I love "Alice".
% I do not love Eve.
"Bob" is born in "UK".
"Charlie" is born in "France".

scenario test is:
    marry_alice expects answers ["I will marry Alice"].
    marry_eve expects answers [].
    citizen_bob expects answers ["Bob is a citizen"].
    citizen_charlie expects answers [].

query marry_alice is:
    I will marry "Alice".
query marry_eve is:
    I will marry "Eve".
query citizen_bob is:
    "Bob" is a citizen.
query citizen_charlie is:
    "Charlie" is a citizen.
